{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "14", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "09", "M": "06", "S": "08"}}, "news": [{"title": "Odisha CM inaugurates two affordable housing projects for urban poor", "para": "Odisha Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi inaugurated two affordable housing projects to support urban poor families. These housing units will be part of a broader initiative under the 'PMAY-Urban BANDHU' scheme. The projects at Ghatikia and Gadakana consist of over 1,600 affordable housing units with extensive facility investments. The government aims to improve living conditions and social status for slum dwellers and their families.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/odisha-cm-inaugurates-two-affordable-housing-projects-for-urban-poor/134936315?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-312216/134936315.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Karnataka high court upholds cancellation of OCs for 33 incomplete villas in Hoskote", "para": "The High Court confirmed the decision of the Samethanahalli gram panchayat to revoke the occupancy certificates for 33 villas in the Raffles Park project, citing substantial non-compliance with regulations. The villas were deemed unfit for occupation as they were incomplete. Following an inspection, the court mandated an investigation into potential misconduct by officials and architects, with possible disciplinary measures pending the inquiry's results.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/karnataka-high-court-upholds-cancellation-of-ocs-for-33-incomplete-villas-in-hoskote/134932076?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-124750/134932076.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "With 90% of its developable land utilised, New Noida to come up in over 20,000 hectares", "para": "The Noida Authority has unveiled plans for a massive 20,000-hectare expansion dubbed New Noida. This venture aims to meet the rising industrial demands and is projected to generate between 500,000 to 600,000 jobs by 2030. The project will kick off with land acquisition in phases, boosting vertical development in established areas.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/with-90-of-its-developable-land-utilised-new-noida-to-come-up-in-over-20000-hectares/134931764?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-254964/134931764.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}